cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use VeriTMM, please cite this software and the optical-constants datasets used by your simulation."
title: "VeriTMM: A verifier-first workbench for multilayer optics"
abstract: >-
  VeriTMM is a verifier-first transfer-matrix workbench for passive, isotropic,
  planar multilayer optics. Simulation, sensitivity, tolerance, robust
  optimisation, and inverse-design results are only reported alongside an
  independent physics acceptance certificate: energy conservation, passivity,
  convergence, cross-solver agreement, and a high-precision referee are checked
  before a result is accepted. Neither an optimiser nor an autonomous agent may
  certify its own output. Results carry typed evidence coverage, a structured
  uncertainty budget that keeps model applicability limits separate from
  numerical uncertainty, and versioned provenance suitable for archival.
type: software
version: "2.0.0"
authors:
  - name: "VeriTMM contributors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Lihonggang-scnu/VeriTMM"
url: "https://github.com/Lihonggang-scnu/VeriTMM"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - multilayer optics
  - transfer matrix method
  - thin films
  - inverse design
  - differentiable physics
  - reproducible research
  - uncertainty quantification
  - scientific software verification
